\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Ah! Lord, with trembling I confess,
\par A gracious soul may fall from grace;
\par The salt may lose its seasoning power,
\par And never, never find it more.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Lest that my fearful case should be,
\par Each moment knit my soul to Thee;
\par And lead me to the mount above,
\par Through the low vale of humble love.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

